  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Probes and Resources: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Probes and Resources: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who Decides What",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Probes==: kubelet health checks on a container",
                "==Requests and limits==: scheduler and kernel contract",
                "==HPA==: changes the replica count",
                "Together: pod is {green:placed}, {blue:kept alive}, {orange:sent traffic}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Probes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Probe",
                "On failure"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Liveness",
                  "kubelet {red:restarts} the container"
                ],
                [
                  "Readiness",
                  "removed from Service endpoints, **not restarted**"
                ],
                [
                  "Startup",
                  "holds off liveness and readiness until booted"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`httpGet`: 2xx/3xx passes",
                "`tcpSocket`: port opens",
                "`exec`: exit code 0",
                "`grpc`: gRPC health check",
                "Each probe runs on its own `periodSeconds` timer"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Requests vs Limits",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Requests",
                  "scheduler **reserves** them when placing the pod"
                ],
                [
                  "Limits",
                  "enforced at runtime: CPU {orange:throttled}, memory {red:OOMKilled}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Liveness vs readiness?** Liveness restarts the container; readiness only stops traffic",
                "**Slow-starting app?** A ==startup probe==",
                "**Readiness fails?** Pod leaves Service endpoints: no traffic, no restart"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Configuring Probes Correctly",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Configuring Probes Correctly",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Key Fields",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Default",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`initialDelaySeconds`",
                  "0",
                  "wait before first probe"
                ],
                [
                  "`periodSeconds`",
                  "10",
                  "gap between probes"
                ],
                [
                  "`timeoutSeconds`",
                  "1",
                  "max wait per probe"
                ],
                [
                  "`successThreshold`",
                  "1",
                  "passes to recover"
                ],
                [
                  "`failureThreshold`",
                  "3",
                  "fails before action"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Startup budget = ==failureThreshold x periodSeconds==, e.g. 30 x 10 = ==300s== to boot"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which Probe Asks What",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Probe",
                "Asks",
                "Gates endpoints?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Liveness",
                  "Should I restart?",
                  "{red:no}"
                ],
                [
                  "Readiness",
                  "Should I get traffic?",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Startup",
                  "Has it finished booting?",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "readinessProbe:",
                "  httpGet:",
                "    path: /healthz",
                "    port: 8080",
                "  periodSeconds: 5",
                "  failureThreshold: 3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Liveness checks a ==database== or dependency: cascading restarts",
                "Short `timeoutSeconds` on a slow app: restart loop",
                "Big `initialDelaySeconds`: use a ==startup probe== instead"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Liveness and dependencies?** Never: one outage restarts every pod",
                "**Size a startup probe?** failureThreshold x periodSeconds above worst boot time",
                "**Default failureThreshold?** **3**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Requests, Limits and QoS Classes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Requests, Limits and QoS Classes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CPU vs Memory",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CPU",
                "Memory"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Unit",
                  "cores / millicores (`500m` = 0.5)",
                  "`Mi` / `Gi`"
                ],
                [
                  "Type",
                  "{green:compressible}",
                  "{red:incompressible}"
                ],
                [
                  "Over limit",
                  "==throttled==",
                  "==OOMKilled==, exit **137**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "resources:",
                "  requests:",
                "    cpu: 250m",
                "    memory: 256Mi",
                "  limits:",
                "    cpu: 500m",
                "    memory: 512Mi"
              ],
              "note": "requests reserve, limits enforce"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. QoS and Scheduling",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Class",
                "Rule",
                "Evicted"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Guaranteed",
                  "requests = limits, every container, CPU + memory",
                  "last"
                ],
                [
                  "Burstable",
                  "at least one request or limit set",
                  "second"
                ],
                [
                  "BestEffort",
                  "none set",
                  "==first=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Scheduler counts ==requests only==",
                "{orange:Pending}: no node with enough unreserved allocatable"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No requests: HPA cannot compute CPU utilization",
                "CPU limit too low: silent latency from throttling",
                "Memory limit below working set: repeated OOMKills"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**CPU throttled, memory killed?** CPU is compressible; memory cannot be taken back",
                "**Which pod is evicted?** BestEffort, then Burstable",
                "**Requests affect, limits do not?** ==Scheduling=="
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Horizontal Pod Autoscaler",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Horizontal Pod Autoscaler",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Formula",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==desired = ceil(current × currentMetric / target)==",
                "Checks about every ==15s==; needs {blue:metrics-server}",
                "CPU % is measured against ==requests==, not limits",
                "No CPU request → metric shows {red:<unknown>}, no scaling"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create and Tune",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl autoscale deployment web --cpu-percent=70 --min=2 --max=10"
              ],
              "note": "or an autoscaling/v2 HorizontalPodAutoscaler"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "v2 YAML: `minReplicas`, `maxReplicas`, `metrics` list",
                "Scale-down waits a ==300s== stabilization window (default)",
                "Scale-up reacts {green:faster}; tune both in `spec.behavior`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Who Scales What",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Changes",
                "Trigger"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**HPA**",
                  "pod count",
                  "metric vs target"
                ],
                [
                  "**VPA**",
                  "pod requests and limits",
                  "observed usage"
                ],
                [
                  "**Cluster Autoscaler**",
                  "node count",
                  "Pending pods"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Desired replicas?** The formula, rounded up",
                "**Why <unknown>?** No metrics-server or no CPU request",
                "**HPA + Cluster Autoscaler?** HPA adds pods; Pending ones make it add nodes"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Troubleshooting CrashLoopBackOff, Pending and ImagePullBackOff",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Troubleshooting CrashLoopBackOff, Pending and ImagePullBackOff",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Reading the Status",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Status",
                "What happens",
                "First check"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{red:CrashLoopBackOff}",
                  "Starts, exits, restarts: 10s, 20s, 40s, max 5m",
                  "`logs --previous`"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Pending}",
                  "Not scheduled",
                  "`describe pod` Events"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:ImagePullBackOff}",
                  "Pull fails, retried with backoff",
                  "Image reference"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Exit ==1== app error, ==137== OOMKilled/SIGKILL, ==143== SIGTERM",
                "Confirm OOM: `describe pod` Last State shows Reason: OOMKilled",
                "Also check whether the ==liveness probe== kills it",
                "Pending: Insufficient cpu, untolerated taints, selector mismatch, unbound PVC",
                "Pull: wrong name or tag, no `imagePullSecrets`, rate limits"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Triage Order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "get pod",
                    "sub": "read status",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "describe pod",
                    "sub": "Events at bottom",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "logs",
                    "sub": "--previous if crashed",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "get events",
                    "sub": "--sort-by=.lastTimestamp",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Reading current logs of a restarting pod, not `--previous`",
                "Guessing resources instead of `kubectl top pod`",
                "Readiness failure shows 0/1 Ready with no restarts"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Pending first?** `describe pod` Events",
                "**OOMKilled or app crash?** Last State Reason OOMKilled; exit 1 is the app",
                "**Why back off?** Growing restart delay stops a tight crash loop wasting node CPU; pull retries spare the registry"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Probes, Resources, HPA and Troubleshooting Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Probes, Resources, HPA and Troubleshooting Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Probes and Resources",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Liveness} restarts the container",
                "{blue:Readiness} gates Service traffic",
                "{purple:Startup} protects slow boots: budget = ==failureThreshold x periodSeconds==",
                "Scheduler uses ==requests==; kernel enforces ==limits==",
                "CPU over limit: **throttled**. Memory over limit: **OOMKilled** (137)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "QoS",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Guaranteed",
                  "requests = limits"
                ],
                [
                  "Burstable",
                  "some request or limit set"
                ],
                [
                  "BestEffort",
                  "none set, evicted first"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. HPA",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ceil(current x currentMetric / target)==",
                "Needs **metrics-server** and CPU requests",
                "Scale-down window: ==300s== by default"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl autoscale deployment web --cpu-percent=70 --min=2 --max=10"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Debug and Status Causes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl describe pod X",
                "kubectl logs X --previous",
                "kubectl get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp",
                "kubectl top pod"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Status",
                "Cause"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "CrashLoopBackOff",
                  "app or liveness probe kills container"
                ],
                [
                  "Pending",
                  "no schedulable node or unbound PVC"
                ],
                [
                  "ImagePullBackOff",
                  "bad image name or missing pull secret"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "Not serving traffic? describe, then logs --previous, then events. {orange:Pending} = scheduling; {red:CrashLoopBackOff}, {red:ImagePullBackOff} = container."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A pod shows `0/1 Ready`, status Running, RESTARTS 0. Which probe is failing, and where is its traffic going?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The ==readiness== probe is failing.",
                "The pod leaves the Service endpoints. It is not restarted, so traffic goes to the other pods."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A startup probe has failureThreshold 30 and periodSeconds 10. The app needs 400s to boot. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The budget is 30 x 10 = ==300s==, so the probe fails first.",
                "kubelet restarts the container, and it loops. Raise failureThreshold to 40 or more."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An HPA targets 60% CPU. 4 replicas run at 90% of their requests. How many replicas does it want?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "ceil(4 x 90 / 60) = ceil(6) = ==6== replicas."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}